      "explanation": "<p><b>Nitrogen Detection (Lassaigne's Test)</b></p>\n<p>Nitrogen in organic compounds is detected by converting it into sodium cyanide, which further reacts with iron(II) sulfate to form sodium hexacyanoferrate(II). By reacting this with iron(III) ions, Prussian blue is formed:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -6.656ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"61.005ex\" height=\"14.444ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -3442.1 26964.1 6384.1\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtable\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtr\" transform=\"translate(0,2692.1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtd\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtd\"><g data-mml-node=\"mstyle\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1472.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2472.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"43\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-43\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3416.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(4416.9,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5444.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(6722.4,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"4E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4E\"></use><use dat